{
  "_readme": {
    "what": "Named lists of structures. group/* tags decide which structures share a group grid (structure_groups.json); every other tag is for grouping, reports and building those lists. Tags have no multipliers any more (2026-09-27: every rate lives in structure_groups.json).",
    "values": "Entries: \"ns:id\" (one structure), \"ns:*\" or \"ns:prefix_*\" (glob, * matches anything including /), \"#tag/name\" (every member of another tag in this file), and a leading \"!\" on any of those to exclude (exclusions win, whatever their position). Unknown ids and tags are errors (logged, listed in the report, and NO structure changes are applied until fixed), so a typo never silently does nothing.",
    "groups": "A structure may be in at most one group/* tag. After changing one, run python3 tools/gen_structure_groups.py to give new members a fitted weight and frequency.",
    "families": "mod/* = one tag per namespace (plus mod/yungs for YUNG's 6). type/* = what the structure is; a structure can have more than one type. dungeon/* = dungeons split by location (surface / underground) and origin (vanilla / better = YUNG's / modded). group/* = the shared grids."
  },
